title: Changes no mark covers
pid: d388093a-a16b-4eee-81a6-6be9d3a89a66
body: |2-
  A commit of the processed makes one check more, from Git
  ('files_hold_more_than_their_node'): a node some changed '.skg' file
  of which, at HEAD or in the worktree, is not byte for byte what skg
  writes for the node as that side's graph holds it (its decomposition,
  each section serialized as the writer does). When both sides are what
  skg writes, the files differ only as the two graphs' nodes do, which
  the leaves cover; when one is not, the files may hold a change no
  graph shows (formatting, a comment). Skg writes every file it saves
  this way, so the check flags only files edited or written by hand. A
  side whose node keeps its text in a section more private than its
  home (overPrivateText) is one skg does not write, and its graph does
  not say which section holds the text, so each file of that side is
  asked only whether it is a section as skg writes one, its parse
  serialized again ('section_is_as_skg_writes_it'); where the text
  moved, the node's other changes say so.
  Such a node is not processed, whatever its marks. A commit of the
  processed leaves it out, and its answer names it, saying that its file
  changed in a way the diff view does not show ("Stage and commit"); a
  commit of everything takes it. The diff view draws no such change:
  the check reads each changed file from Git, which a commit does once,
  and the diff view, refreshed after every save, would do at each.
  A headline's ✓ after ∃ or M says that
  the leaves 'node' names there are marked, and after ~ that the one
  'rel' names is ("What a request names").
